What Is Plank?

Plank is meant to be the simplest dock on the planet. The goal is to provide
just what a dock needs and absolutely nothing more. It is, however, a library
which can be extended to create other dock programs with more advanced features.

(Codenames for releases are currently based on characters of "Ed, Edd n Eddy".)

This repository is a maintained fork of upstream Plank: https://launchpad.net/plank


Building

Build instructions live next to this file:

  COMPILE_CN.md   Chinese, 中文编译指南
  COMPILE_EN.md   English build guide

Both documents list the required packages, the autogen/configure/make steps and
the runtime dependency on bamfdaemon that makes running applications show up in
the dock. To build from a git checkout:

  ./autogen.sh --prefix=/usr
  make -j$(nproc)
  sudo make install

Debian/Ubuntu packages can be produced with:

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b


